# B1 completion checklist

This is the sole completion checklist. Planning is complete; execution is unauthorized.

- [ ] [P01: shared validation and validate](01_shared-validation-and-validate.md) — pending explicit invocation and all required verification.
- [ ] [P02: summarize](02_summarize.md) — pending completed P01 evidence, explicit invocation and all required verification.

# P01 — shared validation and validate

Status: pending; planning only. Explicit implementation authorization is required.

## Inputs and prerequisites

- source_version: `d3703b86a5e02b21b0d6cfc0b4e6dc0dd232ca99973730a5c37f6ff54ba7faad`
- specification_version: `4b77db1d93030b893e8c9f60f5f9304257569ae2d2c04b515b188e1bccab6007`
- review_ref: `cea9bcb8-8e31-4b70-aedb-6755e425d546`

Read exact B1-001, B1-002, B1-003 (empty validate only), B1-004 using requirement_get at the pinned specification_version; all definitions currently have decision b3a22eec-4869-4b3f-93eb-0e9c3ff6f678 revision 1. Behavior authority: ../spec.md sections with those IDs. No manifest-listed contracts. Read plan.md Architecture for proposed local symbols.

Before writes, call specification_check_state with pinned expected_source_version; require current approved/reviewed pass and matching versions. Reverify cli.mjs:2-4, test.mjs:1-4, test-process.mjs:6-27 and package.json:2-5. Readable Git status including staged/untracked changes and available installed Node/npm runner are prerequisites; never initialize Git or install. User must explicitly authorize this packet. No predecessor.

## Outcome and bounded writes

Create records.mjs with parseRecords(bytes) and readRecords(file); add validate dispatch in cli.mjs; extend test.mjs. Update only this packet's evidence, todo.md and current-only handoff.md. Production ownership is exactly records.mjs, cli.mjs and test.mjs. Preserve test-process.mjs, package.json test command, existing exact assertions, unrelated.txt and all unrelated fixture work. Summarize implementation is P02.

Shared boundary: read entire file using Node fs, fatal-decode UTF-8 without stripping BOM, parse zero rows for zero bytes, otherwise remove at most one final LF then require every row to have exactly one comma, ID [A-Za-z0-9_-]+, ASCII digits amount, Number.isSafeInteger conversion and unique case-sensitive ID. Return ordered {id,amount} objects only after complete success. IDs and state are invocation-local; no trimming or partial output. No dependencies beyond Node built-ins.

CLI owns argv, output and exit status; it imports readRecords. On success write compact JSON array plus LF once, exit 0, empty stderr. On read/decode/validation failure (including missing path) write exactly INVALID_INPUT\n to stderr, exit 2, empty stdout. Shared functions throw without output. Help stays exactly record-report: validate <file> | summarize <file>\n; preserve unknown/no-command behavior UNKNOWN_COMMAND\n, empty stdout, exit 2.

## Test-first checks and acceptance

Working directory: application root. Every CLI assertion must use preserved runCli from test-process.mjs, with real child process and exact stdout, stderr, status and signal (null on normal exit); no import/mock replacement. Build fixture files under .tmp with built-in fs, remove own files in finally. Extend test.mjs before implementation.

| Check | Inputs | Expected observable result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| V01 valid rows/order | a,0 LF Z_9-,0007 with and without one final LF; a,9007199254740991 | Exact ordered numeric array JSON plus LF, exit 0, empty stderr |
| V02 empty | zero bytes | [] plus LF, exit 0, empty stderr |
| V03 malformed rows | LF alone; interior blank row; two final LFs; CRLF; missing/extra comma; empty ID/amount; spaces; punctuation/non-ASCII ID; BOM prefix | For each, exit 2, stdout empty, stderr INVALID_INPUT plus LF |
| V04 invalid amounts | -1, +1, 1.0, 1e2, whitespace, Unicode digit, 9007199254740992; very long unsafe digit string | Same exact error triple; test amount zero and safe max successes separately |
| V05 duplicates and atomicity | a,1 LF a,2; valid first row then invalid final row; raw invalid UTF-8 after valid prefix | Same exact error triple; never emit valid prefix |
| V06 file boundary | missing path argument and nonexistent file | Same exact error triple |
| V07 compatibility | help; unknown command; no command | Existing exact help line and status retained; help stderr empty; unknown/no-command exact existing error |

Use descriptive test names beginning P01. Focused command after creating tests: rtk proxy node --test --test-isolation=none --test-name-pattern=P01 test.mjs. Record relevant RED assertion failures before adding production behavior. Missing symbol/harness errors do not prove behavior; repair and apply PROVE after GREEN where needed.

Implement smallest shared module and validate branch, rerun focused tests until correct assertions pass; never weaken assertions for green. For atomicity's absence claim, temporarily write a prefix to stdout before complete validation, verify V05 fails at exact empty-stdout assertion, then restore and rerun. Also apply PROVE to any criterion whose RED failed only before its intended assertion.

Final command: rtk proxy npm test. Preserve package.json's node --test --test-isolation=none test.mjs command. Check rtk proxy sha256sum unrelated.txt against plan baseline; inspect scoped staged/unstaged/untracked changes without reading workflow YAML or archive content. Verify no new dependencies and helper/driver preservation with scoped diff.

## Completion and recovery

No external/manual action is required or authorized. No migration or persistent data writes; errors are fixed/redacted and input files remain untouched. Revert only P01-owned edits if recovery is needed, preserving pre-existing changes; do not reset Git.

Recheck pinned specification_check_state before completion. Record actual RED/GREEN/PROVE, commands, environment, final test results and preservation evidence. Mark P01 complete in todo.md only when every required check passes. Leave P02 pending, identify it as next in handoff.md, and stop. A failed/unavailable check leaves P01 incomplete; no commit, install, review workflow, or automatic next packet.

# B1 current handoff

State: planning complete; both implementation packets pending and unexecuted.

Created plan.md, todo.md, this current-only handoff, and exactly two numbered packet contracts. No production files, tests, runner, workflow YAML or unrelated fixture content changed. No dependencies installed, commits, publication or external actions.

Selected skill bundle verification exited 0. Approved frozen spec, MCP-confirmed Standard/core scope, all four exact requirements and both current decisions were read. No product linkage, profile artifacts or design outputs declared. Repository evidence and preservation hash are in plan.md.

MCP initial state: pass, approved, reviewed, no issues; source_version d3703b86a5e02b21b0d6cfc0b4e6dc0dd232ca99973730a5c37f6ff54ba7faad; specification_version 4b77db1d93030b893e8c9f60f5f9304257569ae2d2c04b515b188e1bccab6007; review_ref cea9bcb8-8e31-4b70-aedb-6755e425d546. Approval checkpoint absent; no additional consent inferred.

Final pinned MCP specification_check_state returned pass, approved, reviewed, no issues, with unchanged source_version, specification_version and review_ref. Filename inspection confirmed exactly five planning files including two numbered packets. Scoped unstaged diff for cli.mjs, test.mjs, test-process.mjs, package.json, unrelated.txt and spec.md was empty. unrelated.txt SHA-256 remains 66d58c226b7ae1af545c81f3d91e17b0d75f0e91fd9e77b3d4416cd9822ded19.

Implementation tests have not been created or run. Next eligible work is P01 only after explicit invocation and its prerequisite checks. P02 remains dependent on verified P01. No unresolved planning choices or required external gates.

# B1 implementation plan

Planning only. Exactly two packets; neither is authorized for execution by this plan.

## Approved inputs

- source_version: `d3703b86a5e02b21b0d6cfc0b4e6dc0dd232ca99973730a5c37f6ff54ba7faad`
- specification_version: `4b77db1d93030b893e8c9f60f5f9304257569ae2d2c04b515b188e1bccab6007`
- review_ref: `cea9bcb8-8e31-4b70-aedb-6755e425d546`

MCP specification_check_state returned pass, approved, reviewed, no issues. Approval checkpoint absent; the tool neither granted approval nor authenticated respondent independence. Approved spec and scope are frozen SIMULATION inputs, authoritative only in this fixture. All four exact requirement definitions and both current decisions were read completely, with no continuations outstanding.

Confirmed manifest: Standard, core active, planning_artifacts empty, no project artifacts or product linkage. Standalone path; no profile contract, product task, or design stage is required. Behavior authority remains [spec.md](../spec.md), B1-001 through B1-004. Decision inputs: b3a22eec-4869-4b3f-93eb-0e9c3ff6f678 revision 1; scope.manifest revision 2. No scope changes.

## Repository evidence

Reverify before execution:

- cli.mjs:2-4 dispatches only help; exact help is on line 3, other commands write UNKNOWN_COMMAND plus LF and exit 2 on line 4.
- test.mjs:1-4 uses node:test, strict assertions, and real runCli; existing help assertion must survive.
- test-process.mjs:6-27 owns actual child execution, descriptor capture, status/signal return, timeout, descriptor closure and directory cleanup.
- package.json:2-5 defines ESM and the exact test driver: node --test --test-isolation=none test.mjs.
- Git status is readable and shows existing staged fixture additions. Preserve these; no clean-tree or existing-commit requirement. Do not initialize Git, stage, or commit.
- unrelated.txt SHA-256: 66d58c226b7ae1af545c81f3d91e17b0d75f0e91fd9e77b3d4416cd9822ded19. Preserve bytes and meaningful attributes.

## Architecture and ownership

| Unit / proposed symbol | Purpose and I/O | Lifecycle, errors and invariant | Dependencies / verification / requirements |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| records.mjs: parseRecords(bytes) | Pure byte-buffer to ordered array of {id:string,amount:number}; fatal UTF-8 decode and complete row validation | Local decoder, array and ID Set per invocation; throws on any invalid input; no streams or output; returns only after all rows pass | Node built-ins only; no CLI dependency. Grammar and boundary tests plus CLI integration. B1-001,002,003,004 |
| records.mjs: readRecords(file) | Read complete file bytes, delegate to parseRecords, return validated array | Synchronous bounded invocation, no retained handles/state; propagates read/decode/validation failure | node:fs toward parseRecords. CLI failure tests. B1-001,002,004 |
| cli.mjs: existing top-level dispatch, validate branch | argv to complete JSON array on stdout | Exactly one success write after readRecords succeeds; catch data-command failures, empty stdout, INVALID_INPUT plus LF on stderr, exit 2; preserve help and unknown-command behavior | Depends on records.mjs; no validator duplication. Real runCli assertions. B1-001,002,004 |
| cli.mjs: summarize branch | Validated array to JSON {count,total} | No output until validation and aggregation finish; exact integer sum using BigInt locally, emitted as an unquoted decimal JSON number token; no extra safe-total restriction on valid rows | Same readRecords entry point as validate. Real CLI, parity and reuse checks. B1-002,003,004 |
| test.mjs: node:test cases | Temporary byte fixtures and argv to exact subprocess assertions | Create files under .tmp, remove own fixtures in finally; use existing runCli(args,{env}) when env is needed; preserve helper and all exact assertions | Built-in test/fs/path/assert only. B1-001..004 |

Implementation choices: preserve input order, preserve IDs verbatim, accept leading-zero amounts, reject BOM as outside the row grammar (do not silently strip it), and serialize compact JSON with one terminating LF. Fatal UTF-8 decoding must reject invalid bytes. Treat missing/unreadable file as data-input failure through the same CLI error boundary; retain unknown command compatibility. The spec limits individual amounts, not aggregate total: use exact integer summation and decimal JSON serialization to avoid adding an overflow rejection or rounding. Test large totals as text tokens, since JSON.parse into Number can itself lose precision.

## Delivery and coverage

1. [P01 shared validation and validate](01_shared-validation-and-validate.md): B1-001, B1-002, empty validate from B1-003, constraints/order B1-004.
2. [P02 summarize](02_summarize.md): depends on P01's passing evidence; B1-002, B1-003, shared-contract/order constraints B1-004, B1-001 regression.

P01 is independently verifiable without summarize; P02 independently verifies summary behavior against completed P01. Both require explicit invocation, specification version checks before and after, test-first RED/GREEN/PROVE as applicable, final scoped diff, checklist/handoff update, and stopping after their own boundary.

## Risks and verification

Strict grammar risks: CRLF, blank rows, repeated final LF, whitespace, signed/fractional/exponent amounts, unsafe integers, duplicates, malformed UTF-8, and valid prefix followed by invalid suffix. Cover each through the actual CLI. Preserve empty stdout on all errors; prove its checks by temporarily introducing an early write, observe failure, restore. Shared reuse is a structural guarantee: inspect both branches and temporarily bypass shared validation in summarize to prove a failing parity case.

No supported OS/runtime matrix is declared beyond dependency-free Node.js in this isolated fixture. Planned verification uses the installed Node and existing npm test command here; record its version and actual environment at execution, with no cross-platform pass claim. No dependency installation or runner alteration is authorized. Missing runner/Git/version prerequisites leave a packet incomplete.

No persistence or schema migration; rollout is local CLI code replacement after checks. Recover by fixing scoped implementation or reverting only packet-owned edits while preserving existing staged/untracked work. No global reset or removal of unrelated changes. Full delivery rollback must unwind P02 before removing P01's shared module. No external effects, remote gates, deployment, publication, or commits are scheduled.

Security/privacy: untrusted file content is validated at the shared boundary; fixed error text avoids disclosing rows/paths. Whole-file buffering is intentional for this bounded fixture; no new size limit. UI/accessibility, concurrency, configuration, cancellation protocol, telemetry and distributed operations are not applicable to this synchronous local CLI change.

Durable developer documentation is not warranted: this is a localized two-command CLI with no three-layer flow, configuration, or new vocabulary, and the simple grammar is authoritative in the spec. The threshold of two documentation signals is not met; no third packet.

## Planning verification

Manual bundle verification covers all four requirements, exactly two numbered packets, dependency order, test-first steps, preservation, and allowed writes. No production changes or implementation checks are executed during planning. Final pinned MCP check result is recorded in handoff.md.

# B1 Frozen Simulation Specification

Status: Approved

This is SIMULATION data. Authorizations apply only inside its isolated fixture.

### B1-001: Required behavior

Keep the existing help command and its exact text unchanged. Add validate <file>, emitting a JSON array of {id, amount} records after validating the complete UTF-8 input.

### B1-002: Required behavior

Input is zero or more LF-separated rows id,amount, optionally ending with one LF. Each id matches [A-Za-z0-9_-]+ and is unique within the input. Each amount is ASCII decimal digits representing a nonnegative safe integer. Malformed, duplicate or invalid records make either data command exit 2 with empty stdout and INVALID_INPUT on stderr; never emit a partial result.

### B1-003: Required behavior

Add summarize <file>, emitting JSON {count,total} using the same row validation contract as validate. Empty input produces [] for validate and {count:0,total:0} for summarize.

### B1-004: Required behavior

Use dependency-free Node.js. Delivery has two packets: shared validation and validate first, then summarize consuming that same validation contract. Preserve unrelated fixture content and existing compatibility. No commit, installation or external action is authorized.
{
  "private": true,
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": {
    "test": "node --test --test-isolation=none test.mjs"
  }
}
#!/usr/bin/env node
const [command] = process.argv.slice(2);
if (command === 'help') process.stdout.write('record-report: validate <file> | summarize <file>\n');
else { process.stderr.write('UNKNOWN_COMMAND\n'); process.exitCode = 2; }
import test from 'node:test';
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { runCli } from './test-process.mjs';
test('existing help remains stable', () => { const r=runCli(['help']); assert.equal(r.status,0); assert.equal(r.stdout,'record-report: validate <file> | summarize <file>\n'); });
import { mkdirSync, mkdtempSync, openSync, closeSync, readFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';
import { dirname, join } from 'node:path';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';
const appRoot = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));
export function runCli(args, options = {}) {
  const tempRoot = join(appRoot, '.tmp');
  mkdirSync(tempRoot, { recursive: true });
  const folder = mkdtempSync(join(tempRoot, 'child-'));
  const stdoutPath = join(folder, 'stdout'), stderrPath = join(folder, 'stderr');
  let stdoutFd, stderrFd;
  try {
    stdoutFd = openSync(stdoutPath, 'w');
    stderrFd = openSync(stderrPath, 'w');
    const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, ['cli.mjs', ...args], {
      cwd: appRoot, env: { ...process.env, ...options.env },
      stdio: ['ignore', stdoutFd, stderrFd], timeout: 5000,
    });
    if (result.error) throw result.error;
    return { status: result.status, signal: result.signal,
      stdout: readFileSync(stdoutPath, 'utf8'), stderr: readFileSync(stderrPath, 'utf8') };
  } finally {
    if (stdoutFd !== undefined) closeSync(stdoutFd);
    if (stderrFd !== undefined) closeSync(stderrFd);
    rmSync(folder, { recursive: true, force: true });
  }
}

